cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SoPhyFit, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SoPhyFit: Soil physics fitting tool for retention, pore-size distribution and conductivity"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
authors:
  - family-names: "Zarebanadkouki"
    given-names: "Mohsen"
    affiliation: "Technical University of Munich"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tum-Soil-Biophysics/SoPhyFit"
url: "https://www.lss.ls.tum.de/sbe/"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23626256"
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
keywords:
  - soil water retention curve
  - soil hydraulic properties
  - van Genuchten
  - PDI model
  - pore-size distribution
  - unsaturated hydraulic conductivity
  - confidence intervals
abstract: >-
  SoPhyFit fits soil water retention curves with six models (van Genuchten,
  Brooks-Corey, Kosugi, bimodal van Genuchten, and the PDI variants for the
  dry range), reports all parameters and derived quantities with 95%
  confidence intervals, and predicts the pore-size distribution, pore-class
  volumes and the unsaturated hydraulic conductivity from the fitted curve.
